course: dictionary
lesson: 8512
title: Satin: one word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. Satin is a noun for a smooth, shiny cloth. It can also be an adjective that describes something smooth and shiny in the same way.
explain: «She wore a satin dress to the wedding.» The word dress is a clue that satin is a cloth here. Satin is often made of silk or polyester, and people use it for dresses, ribbons and pyjamas.
explain: «Male satin bowerbirds build a stick bower and decorate it with blue things.» There is no cloth in this sentence. The word bowerbirds comes straight after satin, so satin is part of the name of a kind of bird. Always check the words around a word before you decide what it means.
fact: Satin is a smooth, shiny cloth, often made of silk or polyester.
fact: Satin is used for dresses, ribbons, pyjamas and ballet shoes.
fact: As an adjective, satin describes something smooth and shiny, such as a satin finish on paint.
fact: A satin paint finish gives a soft shine, somewhere between matt and gloss.
fact: «Satin bowerbirds» are a kind of bird, so satin is part of a name in that sentence.
exercise: «She wore a satin ribbon in her hair.» What is satin in this sentence? | *A smooth, shiny cloth | A type of rain | A paint with no shine at all | A kind of bird
exercise: «The satin bowerbird decorates its bower with blue flowers.» What does satin mean here? | A smooth, shiny cloth for dresses | *Part of the name of a kind of bird | A soft shine on paint | Very old
exercise: Mum says the kitchen wall has a satin finish. What does satin suggest? | A rough, dull surface with no shine at all | *A soft shine, between matt and gloss | A bright, sparkly glitter | A cloth for pyjamas
test: «Her pyjamas were made of soft satin.» What is the best meaning of satin here? | *A smooth, shiny cloth | Very old | A type of paint with no shine | A kind of bird
test: Which sentence uses satin as an adjective, to describe a surface? | «The satin bowerbird is a kind of bird.» | *«The door had a satin finish that caught the light.» | «Satin is an old word.» | «She bought some satin for a dress.»
exam: «She wore a satin dress to the wedding.» Which clue best shows that satin is a cloth here? | wore | wedding | She | *dress
